/tmp
/out-tsc

/node_modules
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
/.pnp
.pnp.js

.vscode/*
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Claude Code personal settings (machine-specific paths; the shared ones live in .claude/settings.json)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Worker worktrees (isolation: worktree). Ephemeral checkouts, one per writing agent — the branch
# lives in the shared .git and is what gets cherry-picked, so the directory itself is never content.
.claude/worktrees/

# Worker status files. LIVE state, not history: a worker claims one before it writes and closes it
# when it finishes, and the lead removes it at acceptance after folding the substance into the run
# log. The invariant is the product — whatever is in here is either running or dead — and committing
# it would turn that into an archive nobody can read. History belongs in .ai/runs/, which IS tracked.
# Lives under .claude/, not .ai/: this is runtime state (the PID-file category), so it belongs in a
# shared runtime directory outside any one worker's worktree — never inside the data or the unit it
# describes. .claude/worktrees/ above is the existing precedent for this convention.
.claude/status/

# Rendered delta views — the JSON receipt carries the whole proof (sha256 + counts) at ~2 KB;
# the HTML is a 1.8 MB rendering of the same thing, produced even when the delta is empty.
.ai/docs-deltas/*.html
